# Documentation Rules

## After Every Meaningful Task
- Remind the developer to save the prompt + response summary into ai-prompts/<category>/
  Categories: planning, design, implementation, testing, debugging, code-review, documentation
- When a design decision is made, note what to record in design-notes.md

## Required Lifecycle Artifacts (create when their sprint reaches them)
README.md, candidate-info.md, tool-workflow.md, requirements-analysis.md,
acceptance-criteria.md, implementation-plan.md, design-notes.md, api-contract.md,
data-model.md, ui-flow.md, test-strategy.md, debugging-notes.md,
code-review-notes.md, pr-description.md, reflection.md, final-ai-usage-summary.md

## Standards
- Every doc: title, date, and a one-line purpose at top
- Docs are AI-assisted but MUST be reviewed/corrected by the developer
- Never commit secrets in any doc
- Prefer tables and numbered items (FR-1, AC-1) for traceability

## Prompt History
- Follow prompt-history-during-task and prompt-history-sprint-log rules
- sprint-X.X.md files are generated at Quality Gate ONLY
